var e=[{number:`01`,title:`The Platform First`,subtitle:`Leverage Browser Primitives Before Introducing Dependencies`,tenet:`Every third-party package is a technical liability, a bundle weight tax, and an ongoing supply-chain risk. The modern web platform already provides exceptional primitives: CSS custom properties, IntersectionObserver, ResizeObserver, dialog, inert, and Web Workers. Staff engineering begins by exhausting native platform capabilities before reaching for an external abstraction.`,details:[`Prefer native HTML semantic elements and CSS grid/flexbox over heavy layout libraries.`,`Use the Web Crypto API, IndexedDB, and Streams API directly for data-intensive client operations.`,`Evaluate third-party dependencies strictly against bundle cost, maintenance overhead, and security attack surface.`]},{number:`02`,title:`Reactivity as First Principles`,subtitle:`Deterministic State Graphs over Coarse-Grained Tree Diffing`,tenet:`UI frameworks should not guess what changed by continuously re-evaluating component trees. Fine-grained reactive graphs (Signals) model dependencies explicitly, updating only the exact DOM nodes that require reconciliation. This eliminates micro-task churn and guarantees predictable, frame-perfect performance.`,details:[`Model state as a Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) with explicit derivation pathways.`,`Eliminate manual subscription management by binding reactive lifecycles directly to component scopes.`,`Batch state mutations transactionally to prevent visual glitches and intermediate frame tearing.`]},{number:`03`,title:`Accessibility as Architecture`,subtitle:`Resilient DOM Topologies over Superficial ARIA Annotations`,tenet:`Accessibility cannot be retrofitted at the end of a product cycle. It is the foundational architecture of the user interface. When semantic HTML hierarchy, deterministic keyboard focus management, and color contrast invariants are engineered into primitive components, universal access is guaranteed by default.`,details:[`Model modal, dropdown, and combobox focus states as immutable finite state machines.`,`Guarantee 100% keyboard parity for every pointer interaction without exception.`,`Adhere strictly to WCAG 2.1 AAA contrast guidelines across light, dark, and high-contrast modes.`]},{number:`04`,title:`Performance as an Invariant`,subtitle:`Interaction Latency (INP) & Frame Budgets as Hard Contracts`,tenet:`Performance is not an optimization pass; it is a fundamental user experience feature. If an interface drops frames during user gestures or stalls the main thread beyond 50ms, it is defective. Staff engineers establish automated performance budgets, profile memory allocations, and design for low-powered devices under degraded network conditions.`,details:[`Offload heavy data processing, parsing, and cryptographic operations to Web Worker threads.`,`Enforce sub-16ms frame budgets and sub-50ms Interaction to Next Paint (INP) across all workflows.`,`Structure bundle delivery with route-level code splitting, lazy loading, and near-zero critical-path CSS.`]}];export{e as t};